    {
      "block_id": "h3-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Key insight",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "After Phase 3, AgentLoop is already a clean adapter shell — ~19 class-level methods, 1 inner adapter class. The `execute_tool_batch()` stub is the only Phase 3 gap. Beyond that, AgentLoop is an **orchestrator**: it bridges user-facing I/O, provider/model backend, ToolRuntime effects, session persistence, and ConversationRuntime loop policy.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The rename to `OrchestratorLoop` is a one-liner alias. The hardening work is strengthening boundaries and evidence, not moving code.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Phase 4 Objective — Chosen",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Phase 4 — Orchestrator Shell Hardening and Turn Evidence Envelope v1**",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Three tightly-coupled goals:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-11",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Goal",
        "Meaning"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**4A — OrchestratorLoop shell contract**",
          "AgentLoop → OrchestratorLoop alias/rename; adapter protocol formalized; no-loop-regrowth guards"
        ],
        [
          "**4B — ConversationRuntime Turn Envelope v1**",
          "Canonical turn result model with hashes, trace_ids, safe summaries — the turn becomes a first-class evidence artifact"
        ],
        [
          "**4C — HandoffReceipt v1**",
          "`fork()` / subagent spawn produce transfer receipts: owner_before/after, scope, budget, return_condition, trace_id"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These three goals form one convergent phase because they're all about making the orchestrator boundary formal, provable, and evidence-backed. They don't require moving any major code — they require hardening what's already there.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Alternatives Considered",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-14",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Candidate",
        "Rejected/Deferred Because"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Orchestrator rename only",
          "Thin — 4A alone would be a renamed AgentLoop with no new evidence. Combine with 4B+4C for a meaningful convergence."
        ],
        [
          "ContextAssemblyPlan v1",
          "Major new subsystem (context compiler, task-aware sections, symbol indexing). Needs its own phase (Phase 5) after shell hardening."
        ],
        [
          "ProviderArbitration v1",
          "Model/provider routing is stable enough. Evidence/ownership hardening should come first."
        ],
        [
          "Projection/Evidence UI v1",
          "Desktop frontend work — orthogonal. Defer to Phase 4D after shell hardening."
        ],
        [
          "Multi-agent lane governance",
          "Ralph + subagent orchestration rules. Needs handoff receipts first. Defer to Phase 6."
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
